; VU1 microprogram (generated by tools/vu1/gen.py skinclip, do not edit): skinned character batches of a character
; that may cross the near plane or the guard band (vu1_skin_begin decides from the bone origins; fixes TECH_DEBT
; char-6, which dropped such triangles). Skin pass layout and input as vu1skin2.vsm, batches of <= 12 triangles,
; header: 0 {tris, cull mask, textured (1.0 / 0.0), 255.0}, 1 K1 (.w 128), 2 A (.w: has m / f), 3 S (.w: k),
; 4 A+D tag (EOP), 5-7
; TEX0 / TEX1 / TEST, 8 PRIM tag with NLOOP 3 + EOP.
; Per vertex (unpipelined): view = w A pa + (1 - w) B pb; colour = min(K1 + B (A + S max(n . L, 0)), 255 / 128)
; with B = 1 textured, the vertex colour flat (vu1skin2's two formulas); st = st * textured, STQ z 1. CLIP of (x F/G, y F/G, z - 2 near) against
; z, then vu1clip.vsm's core (trivial reject, Sutherland-Hodgman against the planes at 1014, projection, fan, one
; triangle per kick from output slot VI08 = 846 / 919); scratch at TOPS+154.

		.vu
		.align 4
		.global VU1SkinClip_CodeStart
		.global VU1SkinClip_CodeEnd
